### Case IH Steiger 540: Heavy-Duty Articulated Tractor

The Case IH Steiger 540 is a high-horsepower four-wheel-drive tractor produced between 2014 and 2023 at the Case IH plant in Fargo, North Dakota, USA. Designed for large-scale agricultural operations, this machine focuses on high-capacity draft performance and heavy implement management.
...
The tractor is powered by a 12.9-liter, 6-cylinder FPT diesel engine. It features a two-stage turbocharged system with both air-to-water and air-to-air intercooling. The engine delivers a rated power of 535 hp, with a maximum output reaching 605 hp. It utilizes an electronic high-pressure common rail fuel system and Selective Catalytic Reduction (SCR) technology to meet Tier 4 emission standards. Power is delivered through a full power shift transmission providing 16 forward and 2 reverse gears.
...
Equipped with a pressure flow-compensated hydraulic system, the Steiger 540 offers a standard pump flow of 42 gpm. Operators can configure the tractor with high-flow options, reaching up to 57 gpm or 113 gpm with the TwinFlow setup, supporting between 4 and 8 hydraulic valves. The rear hitch is a Category IVN type, with an optional Category V drawbar available, providing a lift capacity of 19,621 lbs at 24 inches behind the lift point.
...
The Steiger 540 utilizes a hydraulic articulated steering system for maneuverability despite its size. It rides on a 154-inch wheelbase and is typically fitted with 710/70R42 tires. The base weight of the machine is 43,855 lbs, with a maximum operating weight capacity of 56,000 lbs. Final drives consist of inboard planetary units, and the vehicle is equipped with hydraulic wet disc brakes.
...
