[1] John Deere StarFire | Premium Positioning Docs
URL: https://docs.premium-positioning.com/guides/agriculture/john-deere-starfire
Connect a John Deere StarFire receiver to RTK Premium corrections over NTRIP.

These steps connect a John Deere StarFire receiver to the Premium Positioning correction network over NTRIP. StarFire receivers have no built-in NTRIP client, so the corrections reach the receiver through an NTRIP-capable modem. They assume you already have your NTRIP credentials.
...
- A StarFire 6000, 7000 or 7500 receiver. The SF1 and SF2 accuracy levels do not support RTK.
- RTK and Mobile RTK activations on the receiver. Your John Deere dealer can confirm or add them.
- An NTRIP-capable modem that delivers RTCM 3 corrections to the receiver's serial port. A John Deere modem works only where your dealer's configuration allows third-party networks, so confirm this with your dealer.
...
- Server or host: rtkpremium.xyz
- Port: 2101
- Mountpoint: COMMON
- Protocol: NTRIP
...
1. Connect the modem: Connect the NTRIP modem to the receiver's serial port, following the modem maker's instructions, and check that the modem has a data connection.
...
3. Enter the caster address and port: Enter rtkpremium.xyz as the host and 2101 as the port.
4. Enter your NTRIP username and password: Type your own credentials exactly as they appear in your welcome email. They are case-sensitive and unique to your account.
...
7. Set the correction source on the display: In the StarFire settings on the display, select the third-party RTK correction source. Labels vary by display and firmware.
