The reaccelerated investment incentive (RII), which was initially introduced in the 2024 Fall Economic Statement, is a temporary measure that reintroduces the accelerated investment incentive and allows taxpayers to claim accelerated first-year CCA deductions. Under this incentive, eligible property acquired after 2024 and available for use before 2034 (referred to as reaccelerated investment incentive property (RIIP)) is not subject to the half-year rule. In addition, RIIP that becomes available for use before 2030 qualifies for an enhanced first-year CCA deduction. The CCA deduction is prorated for short taxation years.
