# Women in the Gig Economy: Socioeconomic and Financial Survey Results from Latin American Platforms 

 This report presents the findings of a survey examining the socioeconomic and financial conditions of women working in the gig economy across Argentina, Chile, Colombia, and Mexico. The study focuses on nearly 1,000 women domestic workers using four different gig platforms: Zolvers, Hogaru, Aliada, and Homely. The survey explores aspects such as socioeconomic profiles, relationships with the platforms, income levels, financial inclusion, and perspectives on savings and credit. The findings contribute to a better understanding of the challenges and opportunities faced by women in this evolving sector of the Latin American economy.

