Abstract 
This article proposes to theorize about platform work through a Brazilian perspective 
focusing on the Brazilian platform company iFood. To this end, it analyzes the operation 
and technical materialities of the application “iFood for Deliverers”, its Terms of Use and 
advertising campaigns, within a context of (re)production of neoliberal subjectivities. The 
article seeks to present different strategies for managing the work of iFood's “partner” 
deliverers to produce new dynamics of precariousness, flexibility and control. 
