In this Element, we survey the phenomenon of democratic backsliding. We start in this section with the conceptual terrain and questions of measurement: how to capture the backsliding process and to identify plausible cases. Our empirical contribution rests on an analysis of backsliding episodes in sixteen countries, with structured case studies contained in the accompanying online Appendix.
