abroad, and (2) agrarian sociopolitical structures that facilitated widespread peas 
ant revolts against landlords were, taken together, the sufficient distinctive causes 
of social-revolutionary situations commencing in France, 1789, Russia, 1917, and 
China, 1911” (1979, p. 154).
