Stretching just 400 meters from end to end, Khao San Road is a small yet powerful strip of energy, art, culture, and grassroots growth. From its quiet dawn to its lively nights filled with music and laughter, this is where both Thais and travelers from around the globe come in search of authentic life experiences.
...
Khao San Road has a long history dating back to 1892, during the reign of King Rama V. Originally a rice-trading district run by Chinese and Thai-Chinese merchants, it transformed in the 1980s into a hub for backpackers—offering affordable guesthouses, local eateries, and an unpolished charm that drew global travelers. So iconic that Lonely Planet has named it one of the must-visit destinations in Bangkok. 

