[4] Thailand Visa for Indians 2026: 30 Days Visa-Free from 15 September (2026-06-15T14:21:48.000Z)
URL: https://www.thailawonline.com/thailand-visa-for-indians-requirements/
The short answer, checked on 3 September 2026: an Indian passport holder enters Thailand visa-free for 30 days (entries from 15 September 2026; entries before that date got 60 days). No consular visa, no visa on arrival, no visa fee. India is on the final 30-day exemption list published in the Royal Gazette on 31 August 2026. You do have to file the free Thailand Digital Arrival Card before you travel.
...
It is now law. The Ministry of Interior announcements were published in the Royal Gazette on 31 August 2026 (Volume 143, Special Part 207 Ngor) and name no date: each closes by coming into force when fifteen days from publication have elapsed. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs, in the Department of Consular Affairs summary it published on 1 September 2026, states in Thai and in English that the measures are effective from 15 September 2026, and the Tourism Authority of Thailand says the same. Plan on 15 September. So the 60-day exemption applies to entries up to 14 September 2026, and the 30-day exemption applies to entries from 15 September 2026. India is item 23 on the final list of 60 countries and territories.
...
For tourism, Indian passport holders do not need a traditional consular visa. India is on Thailand’s visa-exemption list, which gives up to 60 days for entries before 15 September 2026 and 30 days for entries from that date, with no visa fee. But “visa-free” no longer means “just show up”: pre-arrival steps apply.

- TDAC, mandatory now. The Thailand Digital Arrival Card. You complete it online within 72 hours before arrival. It is free.
