...
Delivered Energy shall mean the energy produced by a Qualifying Facility and delivered to SRP as determined on a sub hourly basis, expressed in kilowatt-hours (kWh).

Standard Electric Price Plan (Price Plan) shall mean SRP’s published Standard Electric Price Plans (including riders and similar documents) for standard contract Customers, including residential, industrial, commercial, lighting, and pumping Customers. There may be more than one Price Plan setting forth the charges and conditions for a particular customer class or type of service. A Price Plan usually includes an identification letter and number, class of service, character or applicability, prices, conditions, and references to SRP’s Rules and Regulations.
...
QF-24 is available to Qualifying Facilities as defined by 18 C.F.R. §§ 292.101 to 292.207, that provide energy and, as applicable, capacity to SRP and that meet each of the following conditions:

• Have Qualifying Facility status under 18 CFR Part 292; 
• Receive electric service from SRP under a Price Plan; and 
• Have a design capacity of 100 kW or less. 

