Capture One 24.2, released on June 18, 2024, delivers native support for Hasselblad’s entire current-generation medium format RAW ecosystem—specifically the X2D 100C (100MP BSI CMOS), X1D II 50C (50MP CMOS), and 907X Special Edition (50MP back-compatible with V-system lenses). This isn’t limited to basic decoding: users gain full access to Hasselblad’s proprietary 16-bit linear RAW data, including accurate rendering of the camera’s 15-stop dynamic range, native ISO 64–12800 sensitivity curves, and precise sensor-specific noise profiles calibrated against Hasselblad’s own lab benchmarks. Tethered capture—long requested by studio photographers using the X2D with CFexpress Type B cards and the 907X with USB-C 3.2 Gen 2 connectivity—will ship in Capture One 24.3 on September 10, 2024, following beta testing with 127 professional studios across Europe, North America, and Japan between July 1 and August 15. This integration eliminates reliance on Hasselblad Phocus for post-production workflows while preserving critical metadata such as lens tilt/shift parameters from HTS 1.5 adapters and flash sync timing from Profoto C1 Plus units.
