How to tether an IQ4 back with a Macbook Pro over Ethernet and without a DHCP server. · Customer Self-Service
...
It is possible to connect the Phase One IQ4 digital back directly to a Macbook Pro with a standard ethernet network cable and tether to Capture One for Phase One (or Capture One Pro) even without a router or other network devices.
...
It is recommended to use a proper network setup with a router and/or switch with a dedicated DHCP server in place (and optional Power-Over-Ethernet possibilities). However if you for some reason do not have a network to connect too you can still tether using only a standard ethernet network cable without additional hardware (other than a USB-C to ethernet adapter.)

If you have a new MacBook Pro it does not have a dedicated Ethernet port. In this case you will need a USB-C to Ethernet adapter or hub and a regular Cat-5 or Cat-6 ethernet cable (none crossover).

1. Start Capture One and go to the camera tab
2. Power on the IQ4 and XF.
3. Connect the USB-C adapter your MacBook Pro.
4. Plugin the ethernet cable in the IQ4 and the other end into the USB-C dongle.
5. Swipe down from the top on the IQ4 menu, in the "connections" section on the IQ4 menu there should be an IP address listed. (Note: because this in an internal device IP address and your mac is likely not running a DHCP server it will be an address similar to 169.254.Y.X)
6. If the IQ4 has received an IP address from your Mac over the ethernet cable it should now automatically turn up in the Camera tool in Capture One.
...
