- The Law: “…if the goods or the tender of delivery fail in any respect to conform to the contract, the buyer may (a) reject the whole; or (b) accept the whole; or © accept any commercial unit or units and reject the rest.”
- Plain English Explanation: This is the powerful Perfect Tender Rule. It means the seller must deliver goods that match the contract terms perfectly. If the 500 blue widgets you ordered arrive as 499 blue widgets and 1 red one, you have the legal right to reject the entire shipment. The non-conformity doesn't have to be massive; any deviation gives the buyer these three choices.
