## About Master Economie — M1 Economics (PR628)
...
EUR per year
...
Economics as a field of study examines how individuals, firms, and governments allocate scarce resources, encompassing microeconomic analysis of markets and decision-making alongside macroeconomic study of growth, inflation, employment, and public policy. The Master Economie at Université Paris-Saclay, based in Gif Sur Yvette, France, includes a component titled M1 Economics (PR628), reflecting the first year of the master's cycle and its focus on core economic theory and quantitative methods. Students in economics master's programs typically work through microeconomic and macroeconomic theory, econometrics, statistics, and applied analysis of markets, labor, trade, or public finance, building the analytical and quantitative skills needed to interpret economic data and evaluate policy. Graduates of economics master's programs pursue careers in banking, finance, economic consulting, market research, public administration, international organizations, and corporate strategy, while some continue toward doctoral study or specialized research roles. The degree runs for two years, is taught in French, and begins in September, with yearly tuition of 250 EUR. Students considering this program should have a solid grounding in mathematics and statistics along with proficiency in French, since economics at the master's level relies heavily on formal modeling, data analysis, and the interpretation of quantitative results across coursework and applied projects throughout the two years of study.
