The France Excellence Charpak Master Scholarship is the French government's scholarship programme in India, managed by Campus France India and the French Embassy in India. It is limited to Indian citizens and OCI card holders and is not open to other nationalities. It is partial funding: it provides a monthly living allowance of €860 along with visa and Campus France fee exemptions, social security, and additional health insurance, but it does not cover international airfare. The award is renewable once for two-year programmes based on first-year results. The 2026 cycle is closed (interviews took place in April 2026); the 2027 cycle is expected to open around November 2026 with a deadline around February 2027, though these dates are not yet officially announced.
