• Possibly FPGA-like modules, each module can be configured as a network with both feed-forward and feedback (recurrent) connections 
• Spike based system with address-event coding 
• Hierarchically structured interconnects: locally dense connection + globally asynchronous serial link 
• “self-organized” computing modules at both fine-grained and coarse grained levels 
• Dynamically reconfigurable to adapt to the input data and the given problem (the “context”)

