Abstract—The emergence of hybrid memristor-CMOS tech nologies open a promising way to implement compact neuro morphic systems with dense layers of neurons interconnected through memristive synapses for high-speed and low-power inference applications and online learning. The characteristics of memristors make them especially suited to implement STDP learning algorithms on-chip. Using a 130nm CMOS technology with 200nm-sized Ti/HfOx/TiN memristors on top, we have implemented a neuromorphic core with 64 input neurons, 64 output neurons and 4096 1T1R synapses. Using this core, we fabricated a single-core chip and a 16-core chip with 2048 neurons and 64k memristors. We have implemented a stochastic binary STDP learning algorithm, obtaining perfect recognition in hardware for a 4-letter recognition experiment.
