Accuracy Assessment: The results highlighted a minimal precision drop (about 1%) in the models' performance post-mapping when using ideal conditions. Accuracy was affected by maximum input voltage, where voltages below or excessively high led to performance degradation.

Tile Size and ADC Resolution: Smaller tile sizes (64x64) consistently provided better performance, coupled with optimal ADC resolutions around 8 bits, illustrating the critical relationship between physical configurations and model accuracy.

Stochastic Effects and Device Faults: Increased randomness negatively affected accuracy, especially in CIFAR10. The presence of stuck-at faults in low or high resistance states in memristors had a significant impact, particularly in LRS faults that severely dropped accuracy.

Endurance and Retention Testing: Retention exhibited a modest 3% drop in accuracy, while endurance significantly reduced performance with an endurance rate of 52.47% for MNIST and 36.01% for CIFAR10 after multiple cycle scenarios.

