# Cross-Point Resistive RAM Based on Field-Assisted Superlinear Threshold Selector

IEEE Transactions on Electron Devices. Published: 2015-05-08. 111 citations.
...
We report a 3-D-stackable 1S1R passive cross-point resistive random access memory (RRAM). The sneak (leakage) current challenge in the cross-point RRAM integration has been overcome utilizing a field-assisted superlinear threshold selector. The selector offers high selectivity of >107, sharp switching slope of1011. Furthermore, we demonstrate 1S1R integration in which the selector-subthreshold current is102memory ON/OFF ratio and >106selectivity during cycling. Combined with self-current-controlled RRAM, the 1S1R enables high-density and high-performance memory applications.
