The Restatement (Third) of Agency § 7.07 takes a “broader, control-based approach” than the Section 228 framework, but courts have been reluctant to abandon the multi-prong Restatement (Second) analysis. The Restatement (Third) also reinforces related doctrines of apparent authority and estoppel — protecting parties who reasonably relied on the appearance of agency authority based on business cards, uniforms, company email addresses, and representations by the principal (Restatement of Agency Scope of Employment Test).
