The case was heard in theConstitutional Courton 2 and 3 March 2004, with judgment handed down on 15 October. Chaskalson CJ, Langa DCJ, Madala J, Mokgoro J, Moseneke J, Ngcobo J, O'Regan J, Sachs J, Skweyiya J, Van Der Westhuizen J, and Yacoob J were the presiding judges.
The court held that section 23 of the Black Administration Act, in applying the system ofmale primogeniture, was incompatible with sections 9 (equality) and 10 (dignity) of theSouth African Constitution.
