 Mokwele, Ms T 6 Oct 2025 question 

 What (a) number of acres of land has been transferred back to black people since 1994 to date, (b) contribution did each of the programmes of land reform, namely (i) land redistribution, (ii) land restitution and (iii) land tenure reform make towards the land that has been transferred to black people and (c) amount has the State spent on buying land from whites to be transferred to blacks from 1994 to date? 

 Link in context Link 
- 

 Minister of Land Reform and Rural Development answer 

a) The state, through the Land Reform programme acquired and transferred 22.37 million acres (9 052 388 hectares) of land back to black people since 1994 to date.

b) (i) and (iii) Land Redistribution and Tenure Reform programmes contributed 14.82 million acres (5 996 606 hectares).

(ii) Land Restitution programme contributed 7.55 million acres (3 055 732 hectares).

c) The state through the Land Reform programme spent R47 billion on buying land from white landowners and transferred to black people from 1994 to date.

