This work is part of the InTakeCare project. InTakeCare is a modular and scalable framework to monitor medication adherence in chronic patients, designed through a three-tier architecture, which allows easier management, easier scalability and easier implementation of new projects. This architecture is defined by a data tier, an application tier and a presentation tier. The data tier stores and manages the data, allowing for secure retrieval based on the permissions given to each user. InTakeCare uses a non-relational database hosted on MongoDB to store the data, and Amazon Web Services to store the Alexa Skill. The application tier sits in the middle between the other two tiers. It handles the logic and processes the requests. InTakeCare is composed of a single web server, which follows a representational state transfer (REST) architecture. Through HTTP calls to this server, it is possible to access and manage the underlying data. The presentation tier intermediates between the user and the InTakeCare Platform. It is composed by a series of modules, among which are the web dashboard, a smartphone application, a smartwatch application and the Alexa skill. Through the web dashboard the physician inserts all the therapies of the patients. Patients will then receive the corresponding reminder and confirm the medication intake on their preferred module [4].
