After years of waiting, China’s Ministry of Science and Technology (MOST) finally released the final version of the Implementing Rules on the Human Genetic Resources Administration Rules (Implementing Rules) on 1 June 2023, in order to provide further detailed guidance on the implementation of the Human Genetic Resources Administration Rules (HGR Rules) released in May 2019. The Implementing Rules went into effect on 1 July 2023. At the outset, some positive steps are included in the Implementing Rules while following the general trend of China’s human genetic resources (HGR) administration regime and market practices. 

Now, in addition to the Implementing Rules, China has updated its HGR Rules to reflect the change in the authority responsible for HGR management from MOST to the National Health Commission, which took effect on 1 May 2024.
