However, a number of recent China regulations govern various aspects of the collection, use, and transfer of human genetic resources (HGR) and its associated information generated during the scientific studies and clinical trials by the sites in and from China, particularly where a “foreign party” is involved. In this instance, a foreign party must collaborate with a local Chinese partner for these activities. We discuss below some planning considerations in view of recent updates to these requirements.
