Microsoft Genomics (decommissioned on January 6, 2025) was a genomic data analysis service based on the Microsoft Azure cloud platform. The service provided cloud implementations of the Burrows-Wheeler Aligner (BWA) and the Genome Analysis Toolkit (GATK) for secondary analysis of genomes. Its cloud implementations were highly aligned with the best practice pipelines from the Broad Institute.
