directly. If you are using software that submits pipeline execution
requests on your behalf, then refer to that software's documentation on how to
move to using the Cloud Life Sciences v2beta API. Usually, only a
command-line flag or configuration file change is required.## Cloud Life Sciences as a regionalized service
...
The following changes were made to the REST and RPC paths to the Cloud Life Sciences API:
* All paths now use`lifesciences.googleapis.com`instead of`genomics.googleapis.com`.
* All paths now require you to specify a Google Cloud location, such as`us-central1`, when calling the Cloud Life Sciences API.
For example:
...
```
GET https://lifesciences.googleapis.com/v2beta/projects/PROJECT\_ID/locations/LOCATION/operations/OPERATION\_ID
...
Batch requests must be made to regional endpoints:
```
POST https://LOCATION-lifesciences.googleapis.com/batch
```

