# Cloud Healthcare API pricing

Private Preview features that alter operations or stored data that already exist in public Preview are priced according to the Cloud Healthcare API main pricing documentation.

Operations, data stores, and resources that are only available in private Preview features are initially free, and might be billed after they become available in public Preview. Operations, data stores, and resources that are available in both private Preview and public Preview features are priced according to the Cloud Healthcare API main pricing documentation. DICOM data stored in any storage class in Cloud Storage is subject to charge, even in the private Preview release.
...
## Data storage

The pricing tables below show what charges apply when using the Cloud Healthcare API.

For public Preview and GA storage costs, and all other charges, see the Cloud Healthcare API main pricing documentation.

By default, all storage charges are in the Structured Storage category. Storage volume is based on bytes of data ingested plus indexing overhead (as measured by indexed bytes) and backup bytes. Prices are based on periodic measurements aggregated across all data stores during a billing period.

Stored raw DICOM data in all regions uses Blob Storage. Blob Storage prices are based on the amount of non-structured or "blob" bytes that are ingested and stored. Searchable metadata from ingested DICOM images (such as DICOM tags) are persisted and charged as part of Structured Storage.
