3. FinOps Mechanics: Understanding the 2026 Pricing Model

Unlike competitors that charge fixed hourly base fees per database instance, the Cloud Healthcare API uses a pure consumption model. However, its pricing is divided into specific tiers that can trap unprepared teams.

#### Cloud Healthcare API Pricing Breakdown (US Regional Baseline)

- Structured Storage (FHIR, HL7v2, and DICOM Metadata):

- First 1 GiB: Free
- 1 GiB to 1,024 GiB: ~$0.24 per GiB / month
- Above 1,024 GiB: ~$0.19 per GiB / month
- Blob Storage (DICOM Pixel Data):

- Priced at standard object rates: ~$0.02 per GiB / month (with lifecycle options down to Archive rates).
- API Requests (First 25,000/month free):

- Standard Requests(Simple `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `DELETE` by ID): $0.39 per 100,000 requests (drops to $0.29 above 1 billion).
- Complex Requests(FHIR searches with filters, conditional updates, Bundles): $0.69 per 100,000 requests (drops to $0.59 above 1 billion).
- Exporting Data to BigQuery or Cloud Storage:

- Batch Export:$0.19/GiB (first 1 GiB), $0.14/GiB (1–1,024 GiB), $0.09/GiB (above 1,024 GiB).
- Streaming Export: $0.34/GiB (first 1 GiB), $0.29/GiB (1–1,024 GiB), $0.24/GiB (above 1,024 GiB).
