[4] How to set up billing in Terra (GCP) – Terra Support
URL: https://support.terra.bio/hc/en-us/articles/360026182251-How-to-set-up-billing-in-Terra-GCP
Terra runs on the Google Cloud Platform (GCP); all storage and analysis costs are ultimately paid through a Google Cloud Billing account linked to a Terra Billing Project. To make a workspace for storing and analyzing data, you will first need to set up a Google Cloud billing account and link it to Terra. 

Understanding the billing terminology This article uses three related but distinct terms. Understanding the differences before you start will make the steps much easier to follow: GCP Billing Account — A billing account you create and manage directly in Google Cloud. It is connected to a payment method (credit card, bank account, or institutional account) and is the ultimate source of payment for all cloud costs. You set this up in the Google Cloud Console, not in Terra. Terra Billing Project — An internal Terra concept that links a GCP Billing Account to Terra workspaces. When you create a workspace, you assign it a Terra Billing Project; all cloud costs for that workspace are then charged to the GCP Billing Account linked to that project. Terra Billing Projects are created and managed inside Terra, not in Google Cloud Console. Google Cloud Project — A resource-organization concept in GCP that is unrelated to Terra Billing Projects, despite the similar name. Terra automatically creates a Google Cloud Project behind the scenes for each workspace you create. You do not need to manage these directly. See the Terra Billing projects versus Google projects callout in Step 3 for more details.
