[1] Cloud Egress Costs: Reduce AWS, GCP, Azure Fees (2025-04-22T15:00:00.000Z)
URL: https://cloudrps.com/blog/cloud-egress-costs-architecture/
Same-AZ traffic within a VPC: Free. AWS, GCP, and Azure all charge nothing for traffic between resources in the same availability zone inside the same VPC.

Cross-AZ traffic within a region: Not free. AWS charges $0.01/GB in each direction, so a round-trip request-response costs $0.02/GB. GCP charges similar rates. Azure is slightly different but comparable. This sounds trivial until you run the math on a busy microservices cluster doing millions of calls per hour.

Cross-region traffic: More expensive. AWS charges $0.02/GB between regions in the same continent, up to $0.09/GB for inter-continental transfers.

Internet egress: AWS charges $0.09/GB for the first 10TB per month, with tiered discounts at higher volumes. GCP’s Premium Tier egress is tiered as well: roughly $0.12/GB for the first 1TB per month, $0.11/GB up to 10TB, and only $0.08/GB above that, so the headline $0.08 figure people quote only applies at real scale. Azure is similar. For context: Scaleway charges nothing for internet egress, and Hetzner’s free traffic allowance now scales with the size of the instance and varies by region, rather than a flat amount per server. That gap is one reason teams are moving egress-heavy workloads to European cloud providers like Hetzner and Scaleway rather than optimizing within hyperscaler pricing.
